    keySource: "source",
    explanation: "An API key security scheme in the OpenAPI specification defines how the service expects the key to be sent, including the required HTTP header name. The agent can then associate that scheme with the stored project connection and automatically inject the key when invoking the tool. A header parameter only describes an input value and does not provide the authentication mapping needed to use the connection securely. Bearer token security is intended for Authorization headers containing bearer tokens rather than a general API key header."
