    correct: [
      "C"
    ],
    keySource: "source",
    explanation: "Implementing a retry policy with exponential backoff and jitter handles temporary HTTP 429 throttling responses without exceeding service limits. Exponential backoff progressively increases the delay between attempts, allowing Azure OpenAI capacity to recover, while jitter randomizes delays so concurrent requests do not retry simultaneously. Immediate retries can amplify throttling, whereas reducing tools or splitting files does not address model request-rate limits."
