    topic: "Search & RAG",
    prompt: "You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) chat solution used by customer support agents.\nYou are adding an automated pre-production evaluation step to a CI/CD pipeline named Pipeline1.\nThe evaluation will run against a labeled test dataset that contains support questions and the expected grounding context.\nYou need to ensure that Pipeline1 fails if unsupported content or a retrieval mismatch exceeds a defined threshold:\n• responses include claims not supported by the retrieved source content\n• retrieved source content does not align with the labeled expected context\nWhich two built-in evaluators should you use in Pipeline1? Each correct answer presents pat of the solution.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    options: [
      {
        id: "A",
        text: "Retrieval"
      },
      {
        id: "B",
        text: "Fluency"
      },
      {
        id: "C",
        text: "Coherence"
      },
      {
        id: "D",
        text: "Groundedness"
      },
      {
        id: "E",
        text: "Response Completeness"
      }
    ],
    correct: [
      "A",
      "D"
    ],
    keySource: "source",
    explanation: "Groundedness evaluates whether the generated response is supported by the retrieved source content, identifying claims that are not grounded in that evidence. Retrieval evaluates whether the retrieved documents align with the expected context in the labeled test dataset, helping detect retrieval mismatches. Fluency and coherence assess writing quality, while response completeness measures whether an answer sufficiently addresses the question rather than validating its sources."
